1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,088
In the next five lessons,

2
00:00:02,088 --> 00:00:02,724
you build,

3
00:00:02,724 --> 00:00:04,820
ship and run a real online store.

4
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:06,281
It is called CloudCart.

5
00:00:06,831 --> 00:00:08,762
Today is lesson one: you meet it.

6
00:00:08,762 --> 00:00:10,811
You use it the way a customer does,

7
00:00:10,811 --> 00:00:13,210
and you learn every part of every screen.

8
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:14,406
By the end,

9
00:00:14,406 --> 00:00:17,578
you will have started the app on a real Tomcat server,

10
00:00:17,578 --> 00:00:18,401
shopped in it,

11
00:00:18,401 --> 00:00:19,340
placed an order,

12
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:22,101
and answered five questions about what you saw.

13
00:00:22,651 --> 00:00:26,278
No coding today. Just your eyes, your mouse, and a terminal.

14
00:00:27,828 --> 00:00:30,900
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

15
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:35,119
One: start. A real Tomcat server, with the app inside.

16
00:00:35,669 --> 00:00:36,291
Two: look.

17
00:00:36,291 --> 00:00:39,962
A full screen tour of every part of every page: the header,

18
00:00:39,962 --> 00:00:40,584
the cards,

19
00:00:40,584 --> 00:00:41,144
the cart,

20
00:00:41,144 --> 00:00:41,952
the checkout,

21
00:00:41,952 --> 00:00:42,637
the orders,

22
00:00:42,637 --> 00:00:43,819
and the admin page.

23
00:00:44,369 --> 00:00:48,422
Three: shop. Search, filter, add to the cart, sign in, and check out.

24
00:00:48,972 --> 00:00:52,364
Four: your turn. A lab, where one check judges your order.

25
00:00:52,914 --> 00:00:55,255
And the five lessons ahead: meet it,

26
00:00:55,255 --> 00:00:56,555
build it with Maven,

27
00:00:56,555 --> 00:00:57,855
deploy it to Tomcat,

28
00:00:57,855 --> 00:00:59,025
run it and fix it,

29
00:00:59,025 --> 00:01:01,106
then prove it from a clean copy.

30
00:01:01,656 --> 00:01:03,149
Start, look, shop, prove.

31
00:01:05,199 --> 00:01:07,823
Before we click, one picture: how the app works.

32
00:01:08,373 --> 00:01:12,469
On the left, the browser. It shows the pages, and it sends requests.

33
00:01:13,019 --> 00:01:16,987
Next, Tomcat. It receives each request, and hands it to our app.

34
00:01:17,537 --> 00:01:18,522
Inside the app,

35
00:01:18,522 --> 00:01:20,231
a servlet answers the API.

36
00:01:20,231 --> 00:01:22,004
It is a small Java program,

37
00:01:22,004 --> 00:01:23,318
written for the web.

38
00:01:23,868 --> 00:01:27,943
And the data: twelve products, the accounts, and the orders, held in memory.

39
00:01:28,493 --> 00:01:33,229
Browser, Tomcat, servlet, data. Keep this picture. We use it in every lesson.

40
00:01:34,779 --> 00:01:39,750
Go to the lab folder. Type: cd /opt/lab113

41
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:43,198
Look around. Type: ls

42
00:01:43,748 --> 00:01:48,036
The app is already inside Tomcat.

43
00:01:48,586 --> 00:01:50,488
One file: cloudcart.war.

44
00:01:50,488 --> 00:01:52,456
A war file is a whole web app,

45
00:01:52,456 --> 00:01:53,833
packed into one file.

46
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:55,079
In the next lesson,

47
00:01:55,079 --> 00:01:56,522
you build it yourself.

48
00:01:57,072 --> 00:02:02,427
Start Tomcat, and keep the last line.

49
00:02:02,977 --> 00:02:06,902
Tomcat started. It opens the war, and starts the app inside it.

50
00:02:07,452 --> 00:02:17,202
Ask the app for its health.

51
00:02:20,752 --> 00:02:21,444
Status up,

52
00:02:21,444 --> 00:02:23,661
version 0.2.0.

53
00:02:23,661 --> 00:02:24,839
The app is alive.

54
00:02:24,839 --> 00:02:27,749
Now the part a customer sees: the browser.

55
00:02:28,299 --> 00:02:29,079
Open Chrome,

56
00:02:29,079 --> 00:02:30,445
and go to

57
00:02:30,445 --> 00:02:32,590
localhost:8089

58
00:02:32,590 --> 00:02:33,695
/cloudcart

59
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:35,841
This window is private and clean,

60
00:02:35,841 --> 00:02:39,222
so nothing from an earlier visit can get in the way.

61
00:02:39,772 --> 00:02:41,125
This is the home page.

62
00:02:41,125 --> 00:02:42,170
First the header,

63
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:43,523
the bar along the top.

64
00:02:43,523 --> 00:02:44,261
On the left,

65
00:02:44,261 --> 00:02:44,815
the logo.

66
00:02:44,815 --> 00:02:46,229
Click it from any page,

67
00:02:46,229 --> 00:02:47,644
and you come back home.

68
00:02:48,194 --> 00:02:49,128
In the middle,

69
00:02:49,128 --> 00:02:50,130
the search box.

70
00:02:50,130 --> 00:02:50,931
Type a word,

71
00:02:50,931 --> 00:02:52,333
and the shop filters.

72
00:02:52,333 --> 00:02:53,201
On the right,

73
00:02:53,201 --> 00:02:54,203
the menu: Shop,

74
00:02:54,203 --> 00:02:54,670
Orders,

75
00:02:54,670 --> 00:02:55,205
Sign in,

76
00:02:55,205 --> 00:02:56,073
and the cart,

77
00:02:56,073 --> 00:02:58,476
with a counter for the items inside.

78
00:02:59,026 --> 00:03:00,079
Below the header,

79
00:03:00,079 --> 00:03:01,131
the green banner.

80
00:03:01,131 --> 00:03:03,608
Free shipping over seventy-five dollars.

81
00:03:03,608 --> 00:03:05,898
And a reminder: this is a demo store.

82
00:03:05,898 --> 00:03:07,074
Nothing is charged,

83
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:08,498
and nothing is shipped.

84
00:03:09,048 --> 00:03:09,933
Then the hero,

85
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:11,324
the big welcome panel.

86
00:03:11,324 --> 00:03:12,020
A headline,

87
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:12,652
a picture,

88
00:03:12,652 --> 00:03:14,675
and two buttons: start shopping,

89
00:03:14,675 --> 00:03:16,003
and sign in to order.

90
00:03:16,553 --> 00:03:17,567
Under the hero,

91
00:03:17,567 --> 00:03:18,378
the filters.

92
00:03:18,378 --> 00:03:21,621
These round buttons are categories: accessories,

93
00:03:21,621 --> 00:03:22,027
audio,

94
00:03:22,027 --> 00:03:22,702
computing,

95
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:23,378
workspace.

96
00:03:23,378 --> 00:03:24,189
Click audio.

97
00:03:24,189 --> 00:03:26,554
Only the three audio products stay,

98
00:03:26,554 --> 00:03:28,649
and the line below counts them.

99
00:03:29,199 --> 00:03:30,461
Next to the filters,

100
00:03:30,461 --> 00:03:31,345
the sort menu.

101
00:03:31,345 --> 00:03:32,165
Choose price,

102
00:03:32,165 --> 00:03:32,923
low to high,

103
00:03:32,923 --> 00:03:35,258
and the cheapest speaker comes first.

104
00:03:35,258 --> 00:03:36,899
Sorting changes the order,

105
00:03:36,899 --> 00:03:38,098
never the products.

106
00:03:38,098 --> 00:03:39,107
Choose featured,

107
00:03:39,107 --> 00:03:39,802
to go back.

108
00:03:41,652 --> 00:03:46,260
Click all, and scroll down to the product grid. Twelve products, in rows of four.

109
00:03:50,010 --> 00:03:52,093
Every card has the same parts.

110
00:03:52,093 --> 00:03:52,926
The picture.

111
00:03:52,926 --> 00:03:54,523
A small category label.

112
00:03:54,523 --> 00:03:55,703
The product name.

113
00:03:55,703 --> 00:03:56,745
And the rating,

114
00:03:56,745 --> 00:03:57,370
in stars.

115
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,330
Then the stock tag: green means in stock.

116
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:02,800
And the bottom row: the price on the left,

117
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:05,152
and the add to cart button on the right.

118
00:04:05,702 --> 00:04:07,693
Not every product can be bought.

119
00:04:07,693 --> 00:04:09,623
This red tag says out of stock.

120
00:04:09,623 --> 00:04:12,112
The button turns grey and says sold out.

121
00:04:12,112 --> 00:04:13,979
You cannot add it to the cart.

122
00:04:14,529 --> 00:04:15,763
And this yellow tag,

123
00:04:15,763 --> 00:04:17,675
on the webcam: only three left.

124
00:04:17,675 --> 00:04:19,402
A warning that stock is low.

125
00:04:19,402 --> 00:04:21,129
Remember these two products.

126
00:04:21,129 --> 00:04:22,486
They are in your task.

127
00:04:23,036 --> 00:04:25,249
Click a product to open its page.

128
00:04:25,249 --> 00:04:29,741
We choose the USB-C hub: a small adapter with ports for a screen,

129
00:04:29,741 --> 00:04:30,210
a card,

130
00:04:30,210 --> 00:04:31,149
and a charger.

131
00:04:31,149 --> 00:04:32,423
Go back to the top,

132
00:04:32,423 --> 00:04:33,496
scroll a little,

133
00:04:33,496 --> 00:04:34,770
and click its name.

134
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,399
The product page.

135
00:04:36,399 --> 00:04:37,097
At the top,

136
00:04:37,097 --> 00:04:39,001
the breadcrumb: where you are,

137
00:04:39,001 --> 00:04:39,952
and a way back.

138
00:04:39,952 --> 00:04:41,095
The large picture.

139
00:04:41,095 --> 00:04:41,666
The name,

140
00:04:41,666 --> 00:04:42,364
the rating,

141
00:04:42,364 --> 00:04:43,506
and the stock tag.

142
00:04:43,506 --> 00:04:44,141
The price.

143
00:04:44,141 --> 00:04:45,410
And the description.

144
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:46,363
Below,

145
00:04:46,363 --> 00:04:47,773
the quantity buttons,

146
00:04:47,773 --> 00:04:48,781
minus and plus.

147
00:04:48,781 --> 00:04:49,922
Then add to cart.

148
00:04:49,922 --> 00:04:52,407
Look at the cart icon: a one appears.

149
00:04:52,407 --> 00:04:55,026
The counter shows what is in your cart,

150
00:04:55,026 --> 00:04:55,966
on every page.

151
00:04:56,516 --> 00:04:57,401
Open the cart.

152
00:04:57,401 --> 00:04:59,551
One line per product: the picture,

153
00:04:59,551 --> 00:05:00,120
the name,

154
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,068
the price each,

155
00:05:01,068 --> 00:05:02,396
the quantity buttons,

156
00:05:02,396 --> 00:05:03,282
a remove link,

157
00:05:03,282 --> 00:05:05,305
and the line total on the right.

158
00:05:07,055 --> 00:05:07,910
On the right,

159
00:05:07,910 --> 00:05:09,094
the order summary.

160
00:05:09,094 --> 00:05:09,949
The subtotal.

161
00:05:09,949 --> 00:05:11,659
Shipping: $6.99.

162
00:05:11,659 --> 00:05:11,922
Tax,

163
00:05:11,922 --> 00:05:12,842
eight percent.

164
00:05:12,842 --> 00:05:13,763
And the total.

165
00:05:13,763 --> 00:05:17,380
The green bar shows how close you are to free shipping.

166
00:05:17,930 --> 00:05:18,655
Click plus.

167
00:05:18,655 --> 00:05:20,896
Seventy dollars: still five short.

168
00:05:20,896 --> 00:05:21,687
Click again.

169
00:05:21,687 --> 00:05:23,335
One hundred five dollars.

170
00:05:23,335 --> 00:05:24,389
The bar is full,

171
00:05:24,389 --> 00:05:26,037
and shipping is now free.

172
00:05:26,587 --> 00:05:27,503
Click checkout.

173
00:05:27,503 --> 00:05:28,846
You are not signed in,

174
00:05:28,846 --> 00:05:31,411
so the shop sends you to the sign in page.

175
00:05:31,411 --> 00:05:32,510
Two tabs: sign in,

176
00:05:32,510 --> 00:05:33,670
and create account.

177
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:36,720
The dotted box gives you a demo account.

178
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,783
Click fill it in,

179
00:05:37,783 --> 00:05:38,595
then sign in.

180
00:05:38,595 --> 00:05:40,471
A welcome message confirms it,

181
00:05:40,471 --> 00:05:42,284
and you are back at checkout.

182
00:05:42,834 --> 00:05:43,988
The checkout page.

183
00:05:43,988 --> 00:05:44,758
On the left,

184
00:05:44,758 --> 00:05:45,913
the shipping form.

185
00:05:45,913 --> 00:05:46,747
On the right,

186
00:05:46,747 --> 00:05:48,736
a read only copy of your items,

187
00:05:48,736 --> 00:05:49,634
and the total.

188
00:05:49,634 --> 00:05:51,879
Check the details before you order.

189
00:05:53,329 --> 00:05:54,311
Now a mistake,

190
00:05:54,311 --> 00:05:55,082
on purpose.

191
00:05:55,082 --> 00:05:56,905
A street: one Main Street.

192
00:05:56,905 --> 00:05:57,956
A city: Austin.

193
00:05:57,956 --> 00:06:00,971
And a zip code with only two digits: seven,

194
00:06:00,971 --> 00:06:01,392
eight.

195
00:06:01,392 --> 00:06:04,617
Real customers make this mistake all the time.

196
00:06:04,617 --> 00:06:05,879
Click place order,

197
00:06:05,879 --> 00:06:07,772
and see what the shop does.

198
00:06:13,622 --> 00:06:14,764
The form refuses,

199
00:06:14,764 --> 00:06:15,235
in red,

200
00:06:15,235 --> 00:06:18,932
and says exactly why: the zip code must be five digits.

201
00:06:18,932 --> 00:06:22,629
Good errors explain themselves: they say what is wrong,

202
00:06:22,629 --> 00:06:23,839
and how to fix it.

203
00:06:23,839 --> 00:06:24,578
Now fix it.

204
00:06:24,578 --> 00:06:25,721
Select the field,

205
00:06:25,721 --> 00:06:27,872
type seven eight seven zero one,

206
00:06:27,872 --> 00:06:29,216
and place the order.

207
00:06:31,166 --> 00:06:31,489
Done.

208
00:06:31,489 --> 00:06:33,682
A confirmation: your order number,

209
00:06:33,682 --> 00:06:34,327
the total,

210
00:06:34,327 --> 00:06:35,553
and where it ships.

211
00:06:35,553 --> 00:06:37,940
And the cart counter is back to zero.

212
00:06:37,940 --> 00:06:38,327
Click,

213
00:06:38,327 --> 00:06:39,294
view my orders.

214
00:06:39,844 --> 00:06:40,863
The orders page.

215
00:06:40,863 --> 00:06:43,092
Every order you placed: its number,

216
00:06:43,092 --> 00:06:43,665
the date,

217
00:06:43,665 --> 00:06:45,830
each line with quantity and price,

218
00:06:45,830 --> 00:06:46,594
the address,

219
00:06:46,594 --> 00:06:47,486
and the total.

220
00:06:47,486 --> 00:06:48,314
Newest first.

221
00:06:50,364 --> 00:06:51,325
Now the footer,

222
00:06:51,325 --> 00:06:53,120
at the bottom of every page.

223
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:56,069
It shows the version: 0.2.0.

224
00:06:56,069 --> 00:06:58,248
When a customer reports a problem,

225
00:06:58,248 --> 00:07:01,389
the first question is: which version are they on?

226
00:07:01,389 --> 00:07:02,222
On the right,

227
00:07:02,222 --> 00:07:03,953
the link to the admin page.

228
00:07:04,503 --> 00:07:06,317
The admin and health page.

229
00:07:06,317 --> 00:07:08,131
This one is for operators,

230
00:07:08,131 --> 00:07:09,108
not customers.

231
00:07:09,108 --> 00:07:09,875
At the top,

232
00:07:09,875 --> 00:07:10,922
the status: up.

233
00:07:10,922 --> 00:07:12,108
Then the version,

234
00:07:12,108 --> 00:07:13,154
the build time,

235
00:07:13,154 --> 00:07:13,922
the uptime,

236
00:07:13,922 --> 00:07:15,108
the Java version,

237
00:07:15,108 --> 00:07:18,178
and the server: Apache Tomcat 10.1.

238
00:07:18,728 --> 00:07:19,774
Then the memory,

239
00:07:19,774 --> 00:07:21,866
and the counts: twelve products,

240
00:07:21,866 --> 00:07:22,717
one sold out,

241
00:07:22,717 --> 00:07:23,305
one user,

242
00:07:23,305 --> 00:07:24,286
and the orders.

243
00:07:24,286 --> 00:07:26,836
The number matches what we just placed.

244
00:07:26,836 --> 00:07:28,536
This data lives in memory,

245
00:07:28,536 --> 00:07:30,106
so when Tomcat restarts,

246
00:07:30,106 --> 00:07:30,760
it resets.

247
00:07:31,310 --> 00:07:34,702
That is the whole app. Back to the terminal, and stop the server.

248
00:07:38,652 --> 00:07:44,006
Stop Tomcat, and keep the last line.

249
00:07:45,556 --> 00:07:46,324
Stopped.

250
00:07:46,874 --> 00:07:51,952
Is the port free? Count the lines.

251
00:07:52,502 --> 00:07:57,302
Zero. Nothing listens. Everything you saw was a real app, on a real server.

252
00:07:58,852 --> 00:08:02,137
Your task. Use CloudCart like a customer, and prove it.

253
00:08:02,687 --> 00:08:06,527
One: lab up. Start Tomcat, and open the app in your browser.

254
00:08:07,077 --> 00:08:09,290
Two: sign in with the demo account,

255
00:08:09,290 --> 00:08:12,072
and place one order: two Dot-Grid Notebooks,

256
00:08:12,072 --> 00:08:14,032
and one Insulated Steel Bottle.

257
00:08:14,582 --> 00:08:16,537
Three: write answers.txt,

258
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:17,254
five lines.

259
00:08:17,254 --> 00:08:18,362
The order number,

260
00:08:18,362 --> 00:08:19,014
the total,

261
00:08:19,014 --> 00:08:20,383
the sold out product,

262
00:08:20,383 --> 00:08:21,817
the low stock product,

263
00:08:21,817 --> 00:08:22,859
and the version.

264
00:08:23,409 --> 00:08:26,545
Four: lab check. Five checks. You need all five.

265
00:08:27,095 --> 00:08:29,741
Five: lab down, and prove the port is free.

266
00:08:31,791 --> 00:08:35,994
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

267
00:08:36,544 --> 00:08:38,192
The lab lives on GitHub,

268
00:08:38,192 --> 00:08:39,359
at it-waves

269
00:08:39,359 --> 00:08:40,938
/devops-ai,

270
00:08:40,938 --> 00:08:42,449
in the folder academy,

271
00:08:42,449 --> 00:08:43,136
/lab.

272
00:08:43,686 --> 00:08:49,126
Two files: lab113.sh, and shortcuts113.sh.

273
00:08:49,676 --> 00:08:50,577
Install it,

274
00:08:50,577 --> 00:08:53,446
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

275
00:08:53,446 --> 00:08:55,331
-m 755

276
00:08:55,331 --> 00:08:57,380
lab113.sh,

277
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:58,610
into /usr

278
00:08:58,610 --> 00:08:59,593
/local

279
00:08:59,593 --> 00:09:00,577
/sbin.

280
00:09:01,127 --> 00:09:06,247
Load the short name with: source shortcuts113.sh. You get: lab.

281
00:09:06,797 --> 00:09:07,926
You need a JDK,

282
00:09:07,926 --> 00:09:08,258
curl,

283
00:09:08,258 --> 00:09:09,387
and the ss tool,

284
00:09:09,387 --> 00:09:11,313
about one gigabyte of memory,

285
00:09:11,313 --> 00:09:16,161
and ports 8089 and 8099 free.

286
00:09:16,161 --> 00:09:17,821
The lab downloads Tomcat,

287
00:09:17,821 --> 00:09:18,618
and the app,

288
00:09:18,618 --> 00:09:19,149
for you.

289
00:09:19,699 --> 00:09:21,466
Lab check judges your work.

290
00:09:21,466 --> 00:09:24,410
Lab down stops Tomcat and removes everything.

291
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:26,504
Only run it on your own machine.

292
00:09:28,554 --> 00:09:30,623
Pass or fail. You need all six.

293
00:09:31,173 --> 00:09:33,755
Tomcat runs the app, and its health says up.

294
00:09:34,305 --> 00:09:37,377
One order has exactly two notebooks, and one bottle.

295
00:09:37,927 --> 00:09:41,425
The order total is seventy-one dollars, seventy-nine cents.

296
00:09:41,975 --> 00:09:45,133
The order number in answers.txt is the real one.

297
00:09:45,683 --> 00:09:48,200
Sold out, low stock, and version are right.

298
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:51,310
Lab down leaves nothing, and the port is free.

299
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:53,161
To pass, all six.

300
00:09:55,211 --> 00:09:56,982
Your turn, on your own machine.

301
00:09:57,532 --> 00:10:00,561
One: lab up, read the task list, and start Tomcat.

302
00:10:01,111 --> 00:10:04,076
Two: open the app, and look at every part we named.

303
00:10:04,626 --> 00:10:07,229
Three: sign in, and place the exact order.

304
00:10:07,779 --> 00:10:09,507
Four: write the five answers.

305
00:10:10,057 --> 00:10:13,044
Five: lab check, until you see five out of five.

306
00:10:13,594 --> 00:10:16,175
Six: lab down, and prove the port is free.

307
00:10:16,725 --> 00:10:18,560
Pause the video, and begin now.

308
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:34,985
Quick check.

309
00:10:35,535 --> 00:10:38,607
Which part of a product card tells you it is almost gone?

310
00:10:39,157 --> 00:10:41,653
Why did checkout send you to the sign in page?

311
00:10:42,203 --> 00:10:44,208
Where can you read the version that is running?

312
00:10:44,758 --> 00:10:47,766
Why does the order list reset when Tomcat restarts?

313
00:10:48,316 --> 00:10:53,543
Objective covered: CloudCart version zero, meet the app. Start, look, shop, prove.

314
00:10:54,093 --> 00:10:56,162
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

315
00:11:06,712 --> 00:11:09,720
Next: the project layout, and the Maven build.

316
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:13,598
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
